{
  "_comment": [
    "The Chinese terminology and register lock.",
    "",
    "This is the file to edit, NOT the prompt templates. It is injected into",
    "every prompt AND used to audit every answer, so a change here moves both",
    "what the model is told and what it is checked against.",
    "",
    "Parallel in purpose to llm/vi/data/termbase.json, which locks Vietnamese.",
    "Written for older Chinese-speaking adults in Australia: Simplified",
    "characters, mainland vocabulary, and the respectful second person."
  ],
  "register": {
    "_why": [
      "Chinese has no neutral second person. Addressing an older adult as 你",
      "is not informal, it is disrespectful -- and 你 is what every model",
      "reaches for, because it is what web copy uses and web copy is written",
      "for thirty-year-olds. Same class of problem as bạn vs ông/bà in the",
      "Vietnamese lane: a correctness bug, not a style preference.",
      "",
      "Enforced twice: stated in the prompt, and audited after generation.",
      "Telling a model not to do something is not the same as it not doing it."
    ],
    "required_address": "您",
    "self_reference": "我们",
    "forbidden": [
      {
        "form": "你",
        "severity": "error",
        "note": "Familiar second person. Use 您 for an older reader."
      },
      {
        "form": "你们",
        "severity": "error",
        "note": "Familiar plural. Use 您 or 两位."
      },
      {
        "form": "亲",
        "severity": "error",
        "note": "E-commerce familiarity. Never to a senior."
      },
      {
        "form": "喂",
        "severity": "error",
        "note": "Abrupt call-out. Reads as rude in writing."
      },
      {
        "form": "哥们",
        "severity": "error",
        "note": "Slang address."
      },
      {
        "form": "老人家",
        "severity": "warn",
        "note": "Can read as patronising in instructions. Prefer 您."
      }
    ]
  },
